Package: termtest
Version: 1.1.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Jake Van Slyke <pkgs@jvs.sh>
Suggests: git, git-delta, xdg-utils
Description: Probe what your terminal and multiplexer actually render
 Reports which capabilities a terminal genuinely supports -- hyperlinks,
 images, colour depth, unicode width, and similar -- rather than what its
 TERM value claims.
 .
 Running the same subcommand inside and outside tmux is the useful move: the
 difference shows what the multiplexer is filtering, as opposed to what the
 terminal itself lacks.
 .
 Everything it probes for beyond coreutils is optional, so the suggested
 packages only widen what can be tested.
